<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balaputradeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balaputradeva was a prince of the Shailendra dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> who became ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> in the ninth century. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grant of the Pala king Devapala records that, at Balaputradeva's request, five villages were granted to support a monastery he had built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nalanda">Nalanda</a>, evidence of the close religious links between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and the Buddhist states of maritime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balaputradeva.jpg" alt="Balaputradeva" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balaputradewa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
